<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>nv1Quake — Quake on the NVIDIA NV1</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/global.css">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/ico" href="../assets/favicon.ico">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="../assets/favicon.ico">

    <!-- SEO -->
    <meta name="description" content="nv1Quake is a community experiment porting GLQuake to the NVIDIA NV1 / Diamond Edge 3D, the 1995 accelerator that drew quadratic patches instead of triangles. Builds for Windows 10/11 (emulated), Windows 95 and DOS. Free, with source.">
    <meta name="keywords" content="NV1, Diamond Edge 3D, STG2000, Quake, GLQuake, NVIDIA NV1, quadratic patches, Windows 95, DOS, retro graphics">
    <meta name="author" content="Abigail — Abnormality Software">
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://abnormalitysoftware.com/apps/nv1quake">

    <!-- Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="software.application">
    <meta property="og:title" content="nv1Quake — Quake on the NVIDIA NV1">
    <meta property="og:description" content="A community experiment porting GLQuake to the NVIDIA NV1 / Diamond Edge 3D. Windows 10/11 (emulated), Windows 95 and DOS builds, free, with source.">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://abnormalitysoftware.com/apps/nv1quake">
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Abnormality Software">

    <!-- Structured Data -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
        "name": "nv1Quake",
        "operatingSystem": "Windows, Windows 95, MS-DOS",
        "applicationCategory": "GameApplication",
        "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" },
        "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Abigail" },
        "url": "https://abnormalitysoftware.com/apps/nv1quake",
        "description": "A community experiment porting GLQuake to the NVIDIA NV1 / Diamond Edge 3D accelerator.",
        "softwareVersion": "@@VERSION@@",
        "downloadUrl": "https://abnormalitysoftware.com/dl/NV1Quake/@@EMU_FILE@@"
    }
    </script>
</head>

<body class="bg-gradient-to-b from-pink-100 to-blue-100 text-gray-900">

<!-- ── Navigation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<nav class="cute-header text-white shadow-lg">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-2 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between">
        <div class="flex justify-center md:justify-start">
            <img src="../assets/banner-150px.png"
                 alt="AbnormalitySoftware Banner"
                 class="max-h-[150px] w-auto">
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center md:justify-end md:mr-12 gap-4 py-2 md:py-0">
            <a href="/" class="nav-link">Home</a>
            <a href="/blog/" class="nav-link">Blog</a>
            <a href="/contact" class="nav-link">Contact</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</nav>

<div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto py-10 px-6">

    <a href="../" style="color: #c468a8; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; text-decoration: none;">← Back to Home</a>

    <!-- ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 mt-6 mb-8">

        <div>
            <!-- PLACEHOLDER ART: the Fragged logo until real nv1Quake art exists.
                 Replace installers/art/nv1quake-poster.png (same file name) and re-publish. -->
            <img src="../assets/nv1quake-poster.png"
                 class="rounded-xl shadow-lg w-full"
                 style="max-width: 360px; margin: 0 auto; background: #fff;"
                 alt="nv1Quake">
        </div>

        <div>
            <h1 style="font-family: 'Dancing Script', cursive; font-size: 2.4rem; color: #c468a8; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                nv1Quake
            </h1>
            <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #9a7aaa; margin-bottom: 1rem;">v@@VERSION@@ — Quake on the NVIDIA NV1 — Free, with source</p>

            <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                GLQuake, ported to the NVIDIA NV1 / Diamond Edge 3D — the 1995 accelerator with no
                depth buffer, no triangles, and a CPU that streams every texel to the chip. It draws
                <em>quadratic patches</em> instead, and everything in this renderer follows from that.
            </p>
            <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
                Three builds: a software-emulated one that runs on a modern Windows PC, and two for
                real NV1 hardware — Windows 95 and DOS.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Community statement (prominent, not a footnote) ─────────── -->
    <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; border: 2px solid #c468a8;">
        <p style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 1rem; color: #5a3a6a; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">💖 A community experiment, made with love</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            nv1Quake is a community experiment created by passionate fans of id Software and NVIDIA.
            These applications were created out of love and curiosity. If either company asks us to
            remove them, we will comply immediately.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #9a7aaa; line-height: 1.6;">
            This is an unofficial project. It is not made or endorsed by id Software or NVIDIA.
            "Quake" is a trademark of id Software. No Quake game data is included &mdash; you need
            your own copy of Quake.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Downloads ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Dancing Script', cursive; font-size: 1.9rem; color: #c468a8; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        ✦ Downloads
    </h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4">
        <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;">
            <p style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">🖥️</p>
            <p style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #5a3a6a; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">Windows 10 / 11 — emulated</p>
            <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; min-height: 5.2rem;">The NV1 chip emulated in software, so you can see what it drew without owning one. Runs on any modern Windows PC.</p>
            <a href="/dl/NV1Quake/@@EMU_FILE@@" class="cute-button" style="text-align: center; display: block;">⬇ Download (@@EMU_SIZE@@)</a>
            <p style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #9a7aaa; margin-top: 0.5rem; word-break: break-all;">SHA-256 @@EMU_SHA@@</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;">
            <p style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">🪟</p>
            <p style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #5a3a6a; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">Windows 95 — real NV1</p>
            <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; min-height: 5.2rem;">For a Diamond Edge 3D / NV1 card with the NVIDIA Windows 95 driver. <strong>Not yet run on real hardware.</strong></p>
            <a href="/dl/NV1Quake/@@W95_FILE@@" class="cute-button" style="text-align: center; display: block;">⬇ Download (@@W95_SIZE@@)</a>
            <p style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #9a7aaa; margin-top: 0.5rem; word-break: break-all;">SHA-256 @@W95_SHA@@</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;">
            <p style="font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">💾</p>
            <p style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #5a3a6a; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">DOS — real NV1</p>
            <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; min-height: 5.2rem;">A genuine MS-DOS installer and DOS/4GW build for the NV1 and NVIDIA's DOS resource manager. No sound. <strong>Not yet run on real hardware.</strong></p>
            <a href="/dl/NV1Quake/@@DOS_FILE@@" class="cute-button" style="text-align: center; display: block;">⬇ Download (@@DOS_SIZE@@)</a>
            <p style="font-size: 0.68rem; color: #9a7aaa; margin-top: 0.5rem; word-break: break-all;">SHA-256 @@DOS_SHA@@</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Source code:</strong>
        <a href="/dl/NV1Quake/@@SRC_FILE@@" style="color: #c468a8; font-weight: 600;">@@SRC_FILE@@</a> (@@SRC_SIZE@@, SHA-256 <span style="word-break: break-all;">@@SRC_SHA@@</span>)
        &mdash; or on
        <a href="https://github.com/MissImprobable/NV1Quake" style="color: #c468a8; font-weight: 600;">GitHub</a>.
        nv1Quake is derived from id Software's GPL Quake source release and is licensed under the GNU General Public License.
    </p>

    <!-- ── What you need ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Dancing Script', cursive; font-size: 1.9rem; color: #c468a8; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        ✦ What You Need
    </h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
        <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;">
            <p style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #5a3a6a; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">Your own copy of Quake</p>
            <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.5;">The installers contain no game data. Copy <code>PAK0.PAK</code> (and <code>PAK1.PAK</code> for the full game) from your own Quake into the <code>id1</code> folder. Quake's data stays copyrighted by id Software.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;">
            <p style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #5a3a6a; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">For the real-hardware builds</p>
            <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.5;">An NV1 card (Diamond Edge 3D, STG2000) and NVIDIA's driver and resource manager. Use <code>-vidmem 2</code> on an Edge 3D 2200 with its expansion modules. The 650,000 texels a frame it asks for is a lot for a period CPU, so start with <code>nv1_subdiv 0.5</code>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Honest status ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Dancing Script', cursive; font-size: 1.9rem; color: #c468a8; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        ✦ Where It's At
    </h2>
    <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <ul style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 1.2rem; list-style: disc;">
            <li>The emulated build is playable, around 22 fps on <code>demo1</code> at 640x400.</li>
            <li>The Windows 95 and DOS builds link NVIDIA's real libraries and are correctly formed, but <strong>have never been run on a real NV1</strong>.</li>
            <li>Known issues: the first-person weapon models still look wrong, textures warp as you move (partly authentic NV1 behaviour), water is opaque, and the hardware sound path has never run.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Credits ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Dancing Script', cursive; font-size: 1.9rem; color: #c468a8; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        ✦ Thank You
    </h2>
    <div class="cute-card" style="padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #7a5a8a; line-height: 1.8;">
            Huge thanks to everyone at <strong>id Software</strong> for Quake, and for releasing the source;
            to <strong>NVIDIA</strong> for the NV1 and an SDK with enough in it to work out how the chip really
            behaves; to the <strong>Quake community</strong> and the <strong>retro gaming community</strong>
            for keeping all of this alive; and to
            <a href="https://www.twitch.tv/carcenomy" style="color: #c468a8; font-weight: 600;">Carcenomy</a>
            for buying an NV1 &mdash; which is what inspired these builds in the first place.
        </p>
    </div>

</div>

